      <VERS vnumber="19"> That thy <gr str="4009">trust </gr>may <gr str="1961">be </gr>in the <gr str="3068">LORD</gr>, I have made <gr str="3045">known </gr>to thee this <gr str="3117">day</gr>, <gr str="637">even </gr>to <gr str="859">thee</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="20"> Have <gr str="3808">not </gr>I <gr str="3789">written </gr>to thee excellent <gr str="7991">things </gr>in <gr str="4156">counsels </gr>and <gr str="1847">knowledge</gr>, </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="21"> That I might make thee <gr str="3045">know </gr>the <gr str="7189">certainty </gr>of the <gr str="561">words </gr>of <gr str="571">truth</gr>; that thou mightest <gr str="7725">answer </gr>the <gr str="561">words </gr>of <gr str="571">truth </gr>to them that <gr str="7971">send </gr>unto thee? </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="22">
        <gr str="1497">Rob </gr>
        <gr str="408">not </gr>the <gr str="1800">poor</gr>, <gr str="3588">because </gr>
